    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116131" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠκύ̆-πους</span></b> , ὁ, ἡ, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πουν</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, τό</span>: acc. masc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠκύπουν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					243
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): 
				Ep.
			 dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πόδεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.383
				</span></i>
			, etc.:—<i>swift-footed,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always epith. of horses, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> l. c., al., and so in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Parth.</u>
				2.44
			</span></i>; of the hare, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				302
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλαφοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					1093
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππικῶν . . ὠκύπους ἀγών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>El.</u>
					699
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					1129
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); of Hermes, Id.<u>Hel.</u> l.c.</div>
